# SPEC: §9, §16
# COVERS: kind:limit
# ERROR_KIND: limit
# EXIT: 1
# TIMEOUT: 30
#
# A longer timeout than the default 10 s, because this case's whole
# job is to run until the VM refuses: under the sanitize and valgrind
# lanes the descent to the call-depth limit is far slower than it is
# here, and a case that is KILLED for taking too long reports as a
# harness failure rather than as the "limit" it was asserting.
# Amendment A1 added "limit" for VM resource exhaustion.  Unbounded
# recursion is user-triggerable, so it raises a catchable value rather
# than aborting -- here nothing catches it, so it exits 1.
fn spin(n) {
    return spin(n + 1)
}
return spin(0)
